Everything below is derived from that project, which is why this repository is
licensed under the GPLv3 (or later) as well:

* `emulator/` is a Go port of `X32.c` v0.88 ("X32 - An X32 Emulator", the
  reference emulator of that project) and of the OSC helpers of `X32lib/`
  (`Xsprint`, `Xcparse`, `Xdump`, `X32Connect`, `validateIP4Dotted`) and of the
  X32Libs.h declarations.

* The command catalogue is mechanically extracted from the command table headers
  of that project (`X32Channel.h`, `X32CfgMain.h`, `X32PrefStat.h`, `X32Auxin.h`,
  `X32Fxrtn.h`, `X32Bus.h`, `X32Mtx.h`, `X32Dca.h`, `X32Fx.h`, `X32Output.h`,
  `X32Headamp.h`, `X32Show.h`, `X32Misc.h`, `X32Libs.h`) and lives in:
    - `emulator/internal/x32/types_gen.go`
    - `emulator/internal/x32/enums_gen.go`
    - `emulator/internal/x32/tables_gen.go`
    - `emulator/internal/x32/sets_gen.go`
    - `docs/x32_commands.json`, `docs/x32_enums.json`
    - `docs/APPENDIX_COMMANDS.md`

* `bridge/` is a re-implementation of the engine of `X32ReaperW.c` v2.86
  (same project), a two way OSC bridge between an X32 and REAPER; the address
  tables, the bank/DCA model and the REAPER side of the protocol come from there.

* `docs/X32_OSC_PROTOCOL.md` and `docs/X32_REAPER_BRIDGE.md` document the
  behaviour of those C programs; the oscilloscope readings, address tables and
  value scales they describe are derived from reading their source.

The upstream C sources and the prebuilt `X32-emulator.exe` are **not** part of
this repository: only this Go implementation and its documentation are.
See the "Credits" section of README.md for how to obtain them.
